.TH STR_TRIM 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
str_trim \- remove leading and trailing whitespace from a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "void str_trim(char *" str );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B str_trim()
function removes leading and trailing whitespace from
.I str
in place, shifting the trimmed content to the beginning of the buffer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
This function does not return a value.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
char str[] = "  hello  ";
str_trim(str);
/* str is now "hello" */
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Haseeb
